<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "The character you chose in a virtual space stands beside your nickname in the chat: in the conversation, in the user list, and on the card somebody sees when they look you up."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_tab_nicklist}>{dgettext("help_features", "Choosing One")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "Enter a space from the conversation toolbar and pick a character. That choice is now remembered for your nickname, so it is still yours the next time you connect — and the chat shows it even when you are nowhere near a space."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_fmt_color}>{dgettext("help_features", "Turning Them Off")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "View ▸ Character Portraits, in the menu bar or the Start menu, switches them off and back on. The plain text line is the other half of what this chat looks like, and somebody reading a busy channel may want nothing but the words."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_warning}>{dgettext("help_features", "Who Has One")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "Only people who have chosen. Somebody who has never walked into a space gets no portrait at all rather than a stand-in face, because a stranger's picture where a person should be is worse than no picture."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_link}>{dgettext("help_features", "See Also")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  <.help_link topic="feature-choose-character">
    {dgettext("help_features", "Choosing a Character")}
  </.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="feature-nick-colors">
    {dgettext("help_features", "Nick Colors")}
  </.help_link>
</p>
